  "findings": [
    "The proposal would establish Mixed-Use Business, Neighborhood Business 1 and Neighborhood Business 2 districts for the North of NERA project area.",
    "Staff reported that data centers and other higher-impact uses would not be permitted under the proposed zoning framework, while existing single-family homes would remain conforming.",
    "The complete supplied minutes report that the motion to place Ordinance 902 on the next regular meeting’s consent agenda for adoption failed 3-4-0; a motion to move the item to the next available business meeting then passed unanimously.",
    "The draft minutes report unanimous adoption of an immediately effective six-month emergency moratorium on acceptance, processing and/or approval of applications to establish or expand detention centers.",
    "The bill is titled as a detention-center moratorium discussion but includes an isolated reference to research on procedures that may apply to data centers.",
    "The bill repeats the data-center wording but identifies the discussion and the anticipated update as concerning detention centers and federal detention centers.",
    "The agenda presents continued introduction of Ordinance 902, options to adopt or not adopt, a Planning Commission recommendation to adopt, and a staff recommendation to schedule adoption on a later consent agenda.",
    "The supplied extracts do not provide its complete signed text or establish an amendment, extension, repeal or replacement of it."
  ],
  "remaining_questions": [
